    {
      "id": "CORE-AWSTGT-VAL-RANGES-01",
      "title": "Out-of-range numeric options are rejected per AWS target with their documented message, and the rest of the pipeline keeps running",
      "tier": "core",
      "priority": "P1",
      "intent": "A typo in one target's BatchSize or Interval must be caught at startup with a message naming the option, not surface as a throttled or silently idle target later. Six AWS targets each carry one out-of-range value - S3 Interval 30 (60..900 s), SQS BatchSize 11 and SNS BatchSize 0 (1..10), Kinesis and MSK Interval 0 (> 0), SiteWise Interval 5 - next to a valid file target. Every message must appear and no AWS writer may start, while the file target keeps receiving records: one bad target does not stop the schedule. MSK Interval 0 being rejected also shows that its 'flush every record' branch (AwsMskTargetWriter.kt:221,368) is unreachable. One invalid target per type on purpose: a writer validates every target of its type (AwsSqsWriterConfiguration.validate), so a second invalid target of the same type would report the first one's message in-process but its own in IPC.",
      "pins": [
        "targets/aws-s3-target/src/main/kotlin/com/amazonaws/sfc/awss3/config/AwsS3TargetConfiguration.kt:127-133",
        "targets/aws-sqs-target/src/main/kotlin/com/amazonaws/sfc/awssqs/config/AwsSqsTargetConfiguration.kt:104-110",
        "targets/aws-sns-target/src/main/kotlin/com/amazonaws/sfc/awssns/config/AwsSnsTargetConfiguration.kt:134-139",
